From 774e66ba4e5edd79e7836245359acdf1f9fb25b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:26:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0079 -- per-tick script-VM/RenderToBackBuffer
 timing

Real-hardware data from patch 0078 (PLAN.md's "40fps push step 3"
comparison, S16FI1/S32FI1, 2026-09-16) ruled out both load-time depth
conversion and per-flip Present() cost as the dominant contributor to
the ~3.6x tick_rate slowdown between 16-bit-forced and 32-bit-native
Shards of God on real HW-486-66 hardware -- both measured directly and
both too small/too cheap to explain it. The two remaining candidates
per that writeup's own interpretation: AGS script VM execution and
RenderToBackBuffer()'s CPU-side sprite compositing.

Read the actual per-tick call structure before writing any bracket
(main/game_run.cpp's UpdateGameOnce()), rather than assuming function
names from memory:

- Script VM execution is NOT one clean call site. It's spread across
  GameUpdateEarlyRepExec()/GameUpdateLateRepExec() (rep-exec-always
  callbacks) and GameUpdateProcessEvents()'s processallevents() (queued
  hotspot/object/region event handlers) -- all of which funnel through
  script/script.cpp's RunScriptFunction(), confirmed by reading that
  function directly. Bracketed the actual VM bytecode call inside it
  (curscript->Inst->CallScriptFunction()), not the whole
  RunScriptFunction() wrapper: PrepareTextScript()'s own function-
  lookup returns early (kScFnRes_NotFound) for the large majority of
  calls (every module without the requested callback is tried and
  skipped every tick), and counting that near-zero-cost miss as script
  execution would swamp the real number.

- RenderToBackBuffer() (gfx/ali3dsw.cpp) IS a clean, single, sequential
  phase, confirmed by reading SDLRendererGraphicsDriver::Render(): it
  calls RenderToBackBuffer() then Present() back to back, never
  interleaved -- Present() is what patch 0035's own DOSAGS_FLIP_INSTR
  instrumentation already measures, so this bracket adds the missing
  other half of one Render() call without double-counting. Only
  invoked on ticks that actually render (main/game_run.cpp: render is
  skipped whenever play.fast_forward or skip_render_and_wait, i.e.
  every DOSAGS_FIXED_TIMESTEP catch-up tick), so its own call count
  will legitimately be far smaller than script_vm's -- documented in
  the new header rather than left as a surprise.

Full-run running aggregates (count/total/min/max via a small RAII
helper, DosPortTickScope, for RenderToBackBuffer's multiple return
paths), not per-call logging and not the flip instrumentation's own
per-100-sample block-and-reset -- a single number set dumped once at
process exit (main/quit.cpp), alongside the existing tick_rate/
frames_skipped/memory_min_free_kb lines:

  DOS-PORT tickstats_script_vm calls=<n> total_ms=<n> min_ms=<n> max_ms=<n> mean_ms=<f>
  DOS-PORT tickstats_render_backbuffer calls=<n> total_ms=<n> min_ms=<n> max_ms=<n> mean_ms=<f>

New file: Engine/main/dos_port_tick_timing.h (DosPortTickTiming struct,
DosPortTickPhaseStats, dos_port_tick_record(), DosPortTickScope RAII
bracket). Wired into main.cpp (shared instance definition, alongside
patch 0078's dos_port_startup_timing), script.cpp, ali3dsw.cpp, and
quit.cpp (final report emission).
---
 Engine/gfx/ali3dsw.cpp             |  14 ++++
 Engine/main/dos_port_tick_timing.h | 115 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 Engine/main/main.cpp               |   5 ++
 Engine/main/quit.cpp               |  22 ++++++
 Engine/script/script.cpp           |  18 +++++
 5 files changed, 174 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Engine/main/dos_port_tick_timing.h

